; ============================================ manas decision — a FRACTAL template (T4)
; T4 of the TEMPLATE LIBRARY (MANAS-SKILL-GROWER.md L249) and its KEY primitive: a
; hand-authored fractal skill that WEIGHS A DECISION — fanning it over the distinct
; CRITERIA the choice should be weighed on (one angle per criterion), then ASSESSING how the
; options fare on each criterion and SCORING them on that criterion, then WEIGHING the
; tradeoffs across criteria into ONE recommendation, then AUDITING that recommendation for
; support. A decision is not made by a single pass; it is made by weighing each criterion on
; its own track and only then combining. It is the audit/backtrack pattern promoted into its
; own reusable skill.
;
; Built at the NARROW-LINE-OF-THOUGHT grain — one focused reasoning move per leaf (not a
; token, not a multi-part question), sized for a 0.5b. Every expert is a read-only
; PRODUCER of a criterion / an assessment / a score / a recommendation / a verdict, so the
; whole fractal runs tiny-model-green.
;
; The shape (the fractal pair, MANAS-SKILL-GROWER L18):
;   decision-flow = flow-branch
;     perspectivist  "emit the decision CRITERIA this choice should be weighed on (one per
;                     criterion: risk/cost/user-impact/...)"          -> ty-perspectives
;     in-ty          ty-doc                                             ; the decision arrives as a doc
;     per-perspective = flow-chain [                                    ; ONE sub-pipeline per criterion
;        decision-assess  "assess how the options fare on THIS criterion — reason it"   -> ty-text  (reasoner)
;        decision-score   "score / rank the options on this criterion, with one reason" -> ty-verdict (auditor)
;     ]
;     backtrack = flow-chain [                                          ; collect + support audit
;        flow-pure (pf-collect-angles "criterion")   ; CODE combiner: joined per-criterion yields
;                                                    ; -> one {kind,target,body} per criterion -> ty-findings
;        decision-audit  "audit the recommendation — supported? any criterion ignored?"    -> ty-verdict (auditor)
;     ]
; flow-ty derives the whole arrow: decision-flow : ty-doc -> ty-verdict (the backtrack's cod).
;
; The CRITERIA are the point: the choice is fanned over its distinct criteria, each weighed on
; its OWN track (never conflated), then the CODE combiner collects them into ty-findings tracked
; BY criterion (target="angle-<n>", one finding per criterion, bodies JSON-escaped). It is code
; because a live 0.5b asked for that structure hallucinated the schema. The auditor then checks
; the RECOMMENDATION: is it supported, was any criterion ignored, is any conclusion a gap.
;
; STRICTLY ADDITIVE — parallel to research.chiral / evidence-sift.chiral / code-test.chiral /
; doc-edit.chiral; research / evidence-sift / code-test / doc-edit / doc-refine / profiles / flow /
; skill are UNTOUCHED. Only new defs live here (decision.chiral) + decision-test.prog + a live
; sample. Every `lens` is ONE small ask (no " and " / " then " / ";" / " & ", <=160 chars,
; non-empty `sees`) so lint-expert returns nil for each — one narrow line of thought per leaf.
;
; Composes:
;   types.chiral  — Expert (+ ctor), Config, Binding (the run surface; imported, never redefined).
;   flow.chiral   — Flow ctors (flow-branch/flow-chain/flow-step) + Ty ctors (ty-doc/ty-text/
;                  ty-findings/ty-verdict/ty-perspectives). The fractal is a VALUE built from these.

(import "prelude/prelude")               ; List, cons, nil
(import "manas/core/types")      ; Expert (expert id lens sees returns slot tools), Config, Binding
(import "manas/core/flow")       ; Flow (flow-branch/flow-chain/flow-step/flow-pure), PureFn (pf-collect-angles), Ty (ty-doc/ty-text/ty-findings/ty-verdict/ty-perspectives)

; ---------------------------------------------------------- the tiny-step experts
; Each (expert id lens sees returns slot tools). LENS is ONE narrow reasoning move
; (lint-clean); SEES is rich context; TOOLS is least-privilege (read only — weighing a
; decision never writes). Ids are unique across the closure (prefixed "decision-" — no
; collision with research's / evidence-sift's / code-test's / doc-edit's pools).

; perspectivist ⊕ : emit the decision criteria the branch fans over (one sub-pipeline each).
; A decision needs distinct criteria — risk, cost, user-impact, maintainability; this names the
; criteria the choice should be weighed on, one per criterion.
(def decision-perspectivist Expert
  (expert "decision-perspectivist"
    "emit the criteria this decision should be weighed on: risk, cost, user-impact, maintainability"
    "{ decision, options, context }"
    "objects, each {kind:\"angle\", body:\"<the criterion to weigh on>\"}"
    "perspectivist"
    (cons "read" nil)))

; reasoner : for THE criterion in hand, assess how the options fare on it — reason how each
; option does against the question from this criterion (a single narrow move). out-ty is ty-text
; (a free reasoning move is PROSE) — NOT ty-findings. ty-findings' seam validator (refine-ok)
; demands a decodable JSON array of objects; a 0.5b's prose reasoning intermittently lacks it,
; refine-failing the seam, and the branch SILENTLY SWALLOWS that per-criterion chain
; (empty-manifest, routing lost) — so the criterion vanishes while manifest-all-green? still
; reads true off the composite. Typing this narrow reasoning ty-text (lenient non-empty,
; research/evidence-sift/code-test/doc-edit's proven-green seam) keeps every criterion on its
; own track.
(def decision-assess Expert
  (expert "decision-assess"
    "assess how the options fare on THIS criterion — reason it"
    "{ decision, options, criterion, context }"
    "a short reasoning: how each option fares on the question from this criterion, and why"
    "reasoner"
    (cons "read" nil)))

; auditor ⊕ : score / rank the options on this criterion — which option wins here — with the
; reason. A per-criterion verdict (a score is a judgment, so it rides the auditor slot).
; `emits` RESTATES what it judged: this is the LAST step in the per-criterion chain and
; chain-run forwards only the last yield, so whatever it does not carry is DISCARDED before
; the backtrack combiner sees it (DC-1b slice 4).
(def decision-score Expert
  (expert "decision-score"
    "score / rank the options on this criterion, with one reason"
    "{ criterion, assessment }"
    "the criterion and how the options fared, then: the option that wins + one reason"
    "auditor"
    (cons "read" nil)))

; NOTE (DC-1b slice 4): there is no `decision-weigh` model combiner any more — the COMBINE is
; code (a flow-pure `pf-collect-angles` in the backtrack, below). A live 0.5b asked to produce
; {kind,target,body} from joined per-criterion scores hallucinated the schema; collecting an
; already-joined list is symbol-manipulation, not text-understanding. The per-criterion
; REASONING stays model.

; auditor ⊕ : audit the RECOMMENDATION for support — is it backed by the scores, was any
; criterion ignored across the weighed findings?
(def decision-audit Expert
  (expert "decision-audit"
    "audit the recommendation: supported by the scores, any criterion ignored?"
    "{ recommendation, criteria }"
    "verdict: sound|has-gaps + one reason"
    "auditor"
    (cons "read" nil)))

; the pool: the 5 tiny-step experts decision fires, in declaration order.
(def decision-pool (List Expert)
  (cons decision-perspectivist
  (cons decision-assess
  (cons decision-score
  (cons decision-audit nil)))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------- the fractal Flow
; per-perspective : a 2-step chain run ONCE PER criterion — assess the options on the criterion,
; then score them. dom = ty-doc (the criterion-injected decision), seam ty-text (the assessment is
; prose; see decision-assess), cod = ty-verdict. Type-checks: cod(assess)=ty-text ==
; dom(score)=ty-text.
(def decision-per-perspective Flow
  (flow-chain (cons (flow-step "decision-assess" ty-doc  ty-text)
              (cons (flow-step "decision-score"  ty-text ty-verdict) nil))))

; backtrack : COLLECT the per-criterion scores (code) -> audit for support (model). dom =
; ty-verdict (the joined per-criterion scores), seam ty-findings (one finding per criterion,
; target="angle-<n>"), cod = ty-verdict. Type-checks: cod(collect)=ty-findings == dom(audit).
(def decision-backtrack Flow
  (flow-chain (cons (flow-pure (pf-collect-angles "criterion") ty-verdict ty-findings)
              (cons (flow-step "decision-audit"               ty-findings ty-verdict) nil))))

; decision-flow : the fractal. flow-ty derives (arrow ty-doc <backtrack-cod=ty-verdict>).
(def decision-flow Flow
  (flow-branch "decision-perspectivist" ty-doc
    decision-per-perspective
    decision-backtrack))

; ---------------------------------------------------------- the tiny-model Config
; binds EVERY slot decision-pool uses (perspectivist / reasoner / auditor) to the
; 0.5b smoke tier — the whole fractal runs on the tiny model. Additive Config; the four shared
; profiles (profiles.chiral) are UNTOUCHED. Selecting THIS config IS the model choice. auditor
; is bound once and used twice (the per-criterion score + the recommendation audit).
(def decision-config Config
  (config "decision-smoke"
    (cons (binding "perspectivist" "qwen2.5:0.5b" 16384)
    (cons (binding "reasoner"      "qwen2.5:0.5b" 16384)
    (cons (binding "auditor"       "qwen2.5:0.5b" 16384) nil)))))
